# Jaagaa accounts allowed to drive THIS machine's relay, in addition to the
# account that claims it first.
#
# Driving a relay runs commands on this machine — git, npm, wrangler, the coding
# agent — as this Unix user, with this user's files. So the grant lives here, on
# the machine, rather than anywhere it could be made remotely: whoever holds the
# hardware decides. jg-api only enforces what this file declares.
#
# One email per line; blank lines and # comments ignored. Re-read on every
# reconnect, so editing this file and restarting the relay is enough to grant or
# revoke. JG_RELAY_ALLOW=a@x.com,b@y.com works too.
#
# Copy to allowed-accounts.txt and add emails. Each account gets its OWN
# workspace tree at ~/Documents/Jaagaa-ai/<account>/<project>, so sessions run in
# parallel without sharing a checkout.

# you@example.com
